proximately 41,300 rooms. The Company also holds non-controlling interests in seven domestic joint ventures. Guided by a disciplined approach to capital allocation and aggressive asset management, the Company partners with premium brands such as Marriott, Ritz-Carlton, Westin, W, The Luxury Collection, Hyatt, Fairmont, 1 Hotels, Hilton, Swiss\u00f4tel, ibis and Novotel, as well as independent brands. Host Hotels & Resorts, Inc. was established in 1927 and was incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James F. Risoleo | President, CEO & Director | Age 69 | Compensation: $5.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 162 people. Revenue per employee of $37.7M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $7.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $160K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Host Hotels & Resorts, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $17.7B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.97\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 101% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0138950619608433},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $23.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Host Hotels & Resorts (HST) vs. The Competition Critical Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/host-hotels-resorts-hst-vs-the-competition-critical-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497457.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company